<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<update comment="Update to omniscape 2.9 that lets ensembles combine Scenarios of different extents, standardizes them by percentile rank, and stops ensemble results carrying the omniscape outputs of a dependency">

    <!-- An ensemble result used to inherit a copy of one dependency's omniscape
         outputs (cumulative current, normalized current, resistance) through the
         dependency merge, so a single species' current maps were presented as
         the ensemble's own results. The Ensemble Connectivity transformer now
         clears them itself; this removes the copies from ensemble results that
         were produced before it did.

         Only the omniscape_outputSpatial row is removed, and only in Scenarios
         holding an ensemble raster. The dependency Scenarios keep their own
         outputs untouched.

         No schema changes: the switch from min-max to percentile-rank
         standardization reuses the existing 'Standardize inputs' option.
         Ensemble results produced before this update keep their min-max values
         until the ensemble is run again. -->
    <action code="Exec" condition="TableExists" criteria="omniscape_outputSpatialEnsemble">
        <item>DELETE FROM omniscape_outputSpatial WHERE ScenarioId IN (SELECT ScenarioId FROM omniscape_outputSpatialEnsemble WHERE ensembleRaster IS NOT NULL)</item>
    </action>

</update>
